  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Government of Vietnam adopted the use of modernised, pressurised water pipe system for 17 water schemes in five provinces. The system allows farmers to directly connect to water piping and irrigate high value agricultural crops using their own pressured irrigation systems. Through the Australia Mekong Water Facility, Australia provided feasibility, design, and construction support for 12 subprojects across seven provinces in 2022.   
&#x200d;
This has increased the capacity of management teams in each Provincial Project Management Unit to design a modernised, pressurised pipeline irrigation scheme that can provide farmers with an improved level of service and increased certainty of water supply.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia-Mekong Water Facility (AMWF) mobilises Australian water and climate expertise to match partner needs in the Mekong subregion.
&#x200d;
In Vietnam, AMWF provided significant input to the drafting of the Law on Water Resources, with Australian experts providing insights and lessons from Australia&#x2019;s water reform experience to the Ministry of Environment and Natural Resources (MoNRE). Vietnam&#x2019;s National Assembly approved the law December 2023. 
&#x200d;
On the successful passing of the law, the Director General of the Department of Water Resources Management (DWRM) of MoNRE noted in a letter to Australian Water Partnership, AMWF&#x2019;s implementing partner, Australia&#x2019;s contribution to the process of having the law amended and to the water sector in Vietnam more broadly.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
